Tectonic v{version}

Track upstream for `flatpak`? (Yes/No)
Yes

`flatpak` overwrites `/usr/share/example/remotes.list`, which `editor` also ships — declare `overrides "/usr/share/example/remotes.list"` in `flatpak` to take the replacement, or rename one of the two

example/
├── modules/
│   ├── flatpak/
│   │   ├── files/
│   │   │   └── usr/
│   │   │       └── share/
│   │   │           └── example/
│   │   │               └── + remotes.list
│   │   └── + module.kdl
│   └── ~ modules.lock.kdl  flatpak recorded
└── ~ example.image.kdl  flatpak added to modules
==== exit 0
